    "updated_at": "2017-12-18T15:58:32Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the clarification!\r\n\r\nIt’s called out twice in that section (`The name is set to anything other than \"html\" (compared case-sensitively)`), and that emphasis led me to wonder if I was doing something wrong by not having any paths where e.g. \"HTML\" could get through. Could be just me, but I think it’s a bit misleading, even if technically accurate, like if it said \"The name is set to anything other than \"html\" (with any whitespace removed)\".",
